{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg1TRZmWpegAqtBS8NqLj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I give up.\n\nThe statement is true, and I checked the math. For n=1 both sides are 1/2. In general, `det(A - Aᵀ)` is `Pf²` of a skew matrix whose upper-triangle entries are i.i.d. with `P(±1)=1/4`, `P(0)=1/2`. Expanding the Pfaffian over perfect matchings, only matching pairs `(M, M)` survive expectation, giving `(2n-1)!!/2^n = (2n)!/(4^n n!)`.\n\nFormalizing that needs a Pfaffian or determinant-over-matchings expansion, an expectation over `2^(4n²)` finite matrices, and a counting argument for `ncard`. I can't do that reliably here with only compiled Mathlib and no way to inspect its sources. I did not modify `/work/putnam_2016_b4.lean`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":515,"cache_read_input_tokens":3606,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":515,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6814b70e-9907-448d-aa28-783547f38ecc","uuid":"f9e52f32-f19f-40b9-a329-a2deb2555b0a","timestamp":"2026-10-14T03:56:33.246Z","request_id":"req_011Cg1TRZRBrWXmhR2kC6WGb"}
